            "title": "Why a Test Kit Cannot Tell You What to Eat",
            "body": "To interpret your results, somebody needs a validated picture of a healthy microbiome. Nobody has one, because healthy people differ enormously. Your sample also shifts with yesterday's dinner, and stool reflects what is leaving rather than what lines your gut wall. No trial has shown kit-guided eating beating generic advice.",
