            "title": "Volume, and the Monotone Trap",
            "body": "Pitch your voice to the back row rather than the front, and check the far corner for leaning or squinting. Then vary it: drop the volume for the confidence, lift it for the stakes, change speed between sections. A monotone is not a personality — it is a nervous system holding very still.",
