            "body": "Fillers are ordinary — a few per hundred words in normal speech — and Jean Fox Tree's 2001 work found 'uh' can even help listeners, flagging that something is coming. Audiences forgive a scattering and barely register it. What they notice is the wall: the speaker who never stops making sound.",
